    <string name="help_title">Help &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="help_how_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="help_how_body">Type your secret message, tap Encrypt, and share the generated link. The recipient opens the link in the app and the message is decrypted using AES 256-bit  once only. After reading, it is permanently and irrevocably deleted from the server.</string>
    <string name="help_security_title">Highest Security (AES 256-bit)</string>
    <string name="help_security_body">All messages are encrypted with AES 256-bit  a standard used by banks and governments. Encrypted data is stored only as ciphertext and deleted immediately after the first opening. No plaintext ever leaves your device.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_q1">Can I read a message more than once?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_a1">No. Messages self-destruct immediately after the first decryption and are irrevocably deleted from the server.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_q2">What happens if I lose the link?</string>
    <string name="help_faq_a2">The message cannot be recovered. There is no backup. Since the message deletes itself after opening, maximum discretion is guaranteed.</string>
